Changes in version 0.3.0 (unreleased candidate)

* Add observed-date rolling lineage analysis and independent checking through
  analyze_rolling_lineage_json() and check_rolling_lineage_json().
* Compare covariance, precision, correlation and partial-correlation rank groups;
  retain tied blocks, explicit missing slots and unresolved internal directions.
* Add founder-specific direct agreement, lag-capped reach, bottleneck bounds
  and checked predecessor evidence. Angular agreement includes equality;
  the existing continuous-history lineage motion semantics remain unchanged.
* Keep point-input numerical enclosures separate from conditional population
  regions. Statistical statements require the caller's declared joint event
  and radius provider; unsupported transfers remain explicitly unavailable.
* Stage coordinated Python/R/Rust version 0.3.0. Native artifact qualification,
  release approval and registry publication remain separate pending steps.

Changes in version 0.2.2

* Remove package-owned Rust build outputs after successful linking so incoming
  checks do not inspect unused standard-library archive objects.
* Restrict Rust archive exports and discard unused sections when linking on
  GNU/Linux. Preserve Rust panic unwinding and existing worker error handling.
* Keep numerical calculations, checked JSON contracts and public interfaces
  unchanged. The published Python package remains at version 0.2.0.

Changes in version 0.2.1

* Support baseline x86-64 checked arithmetic on GNU/Linux and Intel macOS,
  alongside macOS ARM64. The R package no longer requires AVX, FMA or Haswell
  compiler flags.
* Lower the source-build requirement to Cargo and rustc 1.85.1 or later.
  Production Rust dependencies remain bundled for offline builds.
* Expand synthetic R tests for canonical JSON producers and independent checkers,
  including malformed-input and tampered-report rejection.
* Clarify package metadata, dependency attribution and R installation guidance.
  Mathematical premises, report contracts and unresolved outcomes are unchanged.

# eigentrail 0.2.0

* Add checked projector stability, weighted window envelopes, temporal Gaussian
  calibration and conditional positive-definite covariance geometry.
* Preserve history schemas, common-frame behavior and optional witness arguments.
  Geometric stability retains its inclusive threshold; lineage motion retains
  its strict threshold.
